{"tool_name":"phylomda","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"phylomda","home":"https://github.com/liudoubletian/phyloMDA","license":"Not licensed","summary":"An R package for phylogeny-aware microbiome data analysis.","addition_date":"2022-09-04T22:29:57.772013Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T15:42:51.380894Z","tool_type":["Library"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:phylomda","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"neowangtao@sjtu.edu.cn","name":"Tao Wang","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1218-4017","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Chao Zhou"},{"name":"Hongyu Zhao"},{"name":"Huimin Wang"},{"name":"Tiantian Liu"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Phylogenetic inference","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0323"},{"term":"Regression analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3659"},{"term":"Statistical inference","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3658"}]}],"name":"phyloMDA","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/s12859-022-04744-5","metadata":{"abstract":"Background: Modern sequencing technologies have generated low-cost microbiome survey datasets, across sample sites, conditions, and treatments, on an unprecedented scale and throughput. These datasets often come with a phylogenetic tree that provides a unique opportunity to examine how shared evolutionary history affects the different patterns in host-associated microbial communities. Results: In this paper, we describe an R package, phyloMDA, for phylogeny-aware microbiome data analysis. It includes the Dirichlet-tree multinomial model for multivariate abundance data, tree-guided empirical Bayes estimation of microbial compositions, and tree-based multiscale regression methods with relative abundances as predictors. Conclusion: phyloMDA is a versatile and user-friendly tool to analyze microbiome data while incorporating the ph